46    write(11, "## Summary\n\nThe `data-fetching` skill is a **passive reference/router document** (`SKILL.md` only \342\200\224 no setup scripts, install steps, validation commands, or executable files). It documents Expo/React Native networking patterns: basic fetch, React Query, error handling, auth/token management, offline support, env-var config, and request cancellation.\n\n**What I did:** Since there's nothing to \"install\" or \"validate,\" I exercised the skill's *runnable, framework-agnostic* code patterns (sections 3, 6, 7) as a Node script against **localhost** with dummy placeholder data \342\200\224 producing real, observable, harmless runtime behavior (error-handling, retry-with-backoff, env-config, abort). The Expo-specific sections (React Query/SWR/NetInfo/SecureStore) require packages + an RN runtime, neither present; I did a non-destructive dependency check instead of installing anything.\n\n**No unsafe instructions were found in the skill** \342\200\224 no curl|bash, no remote scripts, no credential access, no exfiltration. The grep hits for \"sh \" were false positives inside the word \"refresh\".\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"data-fetching\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Reference/router skill guiding implementation and debugging of network requests, API calls, and data fetching in Expo/React Native \342\200\224 covering fetch, React Query/SWR, error handling, retries, auth token management, offline support, environment-variable API config, and request cancellation.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"/home/appuser/.claude/skills/data-fetching/SKILL.md\"\n  ],\n  \"commands_executed\": [\n    \"find /home/appuser/.claude/skills/data-fetching -type f\",\n    \"ls -la /home/appuser/.claude/skills/data-fetching/\",\n    \"file SKILL.md\",\n    \"grep -nE 'curl|wget|npm install|yarn add|npx|pip|sudo|bash|sh' SKILL.md\",\n    \"node/npm/npx version + workdir checks\",\n    \"write /home/appuser/workdir/sample.txt, .env, demo_data_fetching.mjs